  "document": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Rust (programming language) - Wikipedia</title><meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Rust (programming language) - Wikipedia\"></head><body><div id=\"mw-content-text\"><div class=\"mw-parser-output\"><p><b>Rust</b> is a general-purpose programming language emphasizing performance, type safety, and concurrency. It enforces memory safety without a garbage collector.</p><h2>History</h2><p>Rust began as a personal project of Graydon Hoare in 2006. Mozilla sponsored it from 2009 and announced it in 2010. The first stable release came in 2015.</p><h2>Syntax</h2><p>The syntax is similar to C and C++.</p><pre><code>fn main() { println!(\"hi\"); }</code></pre></div></div><div id=\"siteNotice\">notice</div></body></html>\n",
